            <ArticleTitle>The effect of a peripheral mononeuropathy on immunoreactive (ir)-galanin release in the spinal cord of the rat.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>259-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The pattern of ir-galanin release in the spinal cord of rats with a peripheral mononeuropathy was studied. On the side of the cord ipsilateral to the nerve injury enhanced ir-galanin release was found in the superficial dorsal horn. It is probable that, after nerve injury, some primary afferent neurons spontaneously release galanin from their central terminals.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
